cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spxtacular in your research, please cite the archived software release."
type: software
title: "spxtacular: Mass spectrometry spectrum processing in Python"
abstract: >-
  spxtacular is a Python library for general mass-spectrum processing
  through chainable Spectrum and MsnSpectrum objects. Processing operations
  include denoising, peak filtering, isotope deconvolution, charge assignment,
  neutral-mass conversion, fragment matching, and peptide-spectrum match
  scoring. Deconvolution uses isotope-profile similarity scores and can use
  optional Numba compilation. Matching accepts mass tolerances in parts per
  million or daltons, and scoring includes hyperscore, spectral angle, and
  matched-peak measures. Reader adapters cover Bruker timsTOF directories, mzML
  files, and Thermo RAW files. Separate readers and writers support MGF, MS2,
  and MSP peak lists and spectral libraries. Plotly-based views include stick,
  mirror, faceted, mass-error, annotated-fragment, and sequence-coverage plots,
  together with tabular output for screen readers. Optional adapters exchange
  spectra with matchms and spectrum_utils, while spectrl integration converts
  spectra to and from URL-safe tokens. spxtacular is intended for interactive
  analysis, pipeline construction, spectral-library work, and method
  development across centroided and mobility-aware proteomics, metabolomics,
  lipidomics, glycomics, and oligonucleotide data.
